  ],
  "recordedAt": "2026-06-18T13:00:00Z",
  "contextText": "Planning the clinic-by-clinic rollout of the new intake.",
  "hasTranscript": true,
  "speakers": [
    {
      "id": "m25-spk-a",
      "label": "A",
      "displayName": "Alex Rivera"
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-spk-b",
      "label": "B",
      "displayName": "Elif Kaya"
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-spk-c",
      "label": "C",
      "displayName": "Samir Haddad"
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-spk-d",
      "label": "D",
      "displayName": "Nadia Brooks"
    }
  ],
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m25-s001",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 6300,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks everyone. The build is done for the first clinic, so today is about rollout."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s002",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-b",
      "startMs": 6550,
      "endMs": 16270,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Before that, a quick org note. Since the reorg in May I report to Samir, so clinical and product sit in one team now."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s003",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-c",
      "startMs": 16520,
      "endMs": 19020,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Which makes sign-offs easier, honestly."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s004",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-a",
      "startMs": 19270,
      "endMs": 22150,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Good to know. So, rollout order?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s005",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-b",
      "startMs": 22400,
      "endMs": 27560,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Clinic by clinic. I don't want a big bang across the network."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s006",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-c",
      "startMs": 27810,
      "endMs": 33730,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Start with Eastgate. It has the highest walk-in volume, so we learn fastest there."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s007",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-b",
      "startMs": 33980,
      "endMs": 39140,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Agreed. We roll out clinic by clinic, starting with the Eastgate clinic."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s008",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-a",
      "startMs": 39390,
      "endMs": 43030,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Decided. What does each clinic need before switching?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s009",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-d",
      "startMs": 43280,
      "endMs": 48440,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The front-desk leads need a short training session. Thirty minutes is enough."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s010",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-b",
      "startMs": 48690,
      "endMs": 53470,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll train the front-desk leads at every clinic by July 10."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s011",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-a",
      "startMs": 53720,
      "endMs": 55460,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "And clinical wording?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s012",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-c",
      "startMs": 55710,
      "endMs": 64290,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The final clinical wording on the medication screens still needs my sign-off. I'll sign off the clinical wording by next Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s013",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-d",
      "startMs": 64540,
      "endMs": 68180,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll send you the final screens this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s014",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-a",
      "startMs": 68430,
      "endMs": 71690,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "What about support in the first week?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s015",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-d",
      "startMs": 71940,
      "endMs": 76340,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll sit at the Eastgate front desk on launch day."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s016",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-b",
      "startMs": 76590,
      "endMs": 78710,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's generous, thank you."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s017",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-c",
      "startMs": 78960,
      "endMs": 81460,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "How do we measure success?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s018",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-b",
      "startMs": 81710,
      "endMs": 89910,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Incomplete forms. We started at 40 percent. If Eastgate gets under 10 percent in the first month, we go wider."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s019",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-a",
      "startMs": 90160,
      "endMs": 92280,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Good, a clear bar."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s020",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-b",
      "startMs": 92530,
      "endMs": 99210,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Personal note, I'm relocating to the coast next spring, but I'll stay on this project remotely."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s021",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-a",
      "startMs": 99460,
      "endMs": 103100,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Congratulations, and good to hear you're staying on."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s022",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-c",
      "startMs": 103350,
      "endMs": 106610,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "We'd have fought to keep her anyway."
    },
    {
      "id": "m25-s023",
      "speakerId": "m25-spk-a",
      "startMs": 106860,
      "endMs": 112020,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Great. So: Eastgate first, training by July 10, wording by next Tuesday."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Corvid intake rollout planning\n\n**Date:** June 18\n**Attendees:** Alex Rivera (Larkspur Labs), Nadia Brooks (Larkspur Labs), Elif Kaya (Corvid Health), Samir Haddad (Corvid Health)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe build of the new patient intake is complete for the first clinic. This session planned the rollout across Corvid Health's walk-in clinics.\n\n## Org change\n\nSince Corvid's reorg in May, Elif reports to Samir, so clinical and product now sit in one team. Samir expects this to make sign-offs easier.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Roll out clinic by clinic, starting with the Eastgate clinic**, which has the highest walk-in volume. No big-bang rollout.\n- Success bar: incomplete forms started at 40 percent; if Eastgate gets under 10 percent in the first month, the rollout goes wider.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Elif Kaya** — train the front-desk leads at every clinic by July 10 (about thirty minutes each).\n- **Samir Haddad** — sign off the clinical wording on the medication screens by next Tuesday.\n- **Nadia Brooks** — send Samir the final screens this afternoon; sit at the Eastgate front desk on launch day.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Elif is relocating to the coast next spring and will stay on the project remotely.\n- Nadia's launch-day presence at Eastgate is meant to catch usability problems the test sessions missed.\n"
  },
